// Puzzle data for Outwit, the daily crowd game. SERVER-ONLY: imported by
// app/outwit/page.js (which strips answers/house before the client sees it)
// and by app/api/outwit/route.js (which scores against house + real picks).
// The `house` arrays are the pre-written "house crowd" (~48 answers per
// prompt) that seeds each day's pool so the first player at 12:01am faces a
// realistic field. For choice AND unique prompts, house entries are OPTION INDICES.
// Generated by a seeded script (deterministic); hand-shaped distributions.
// When banking more days: keep prompt types + order (least, herd, match,
// unique, twothirds — unique is a themed 8-option rarest-pick prompt, and the
// twothirds "Undercut" prompt runs LAST), write fresh flavor, and re-shape house
// arrays to plausible crowd behavior for the new questions. Truth/truthNote
// power the herd reveal.
//
// UNDERCUT FRACTION MOVES DAILY (owner rule, 2026-07-20): the Undercut prompt is
// no longer always two-thirds of the average. Each day carries an explicit
// `frac` (and matching `fracLabel` / question copy) drawn from 1/3, 2/5, 1/2,
// 3/5, 2/3, 7/10, 3/4, 4/5, never repeating on back-to-back days, so players
// cannot memorize one equilibrium. `frac` is what lib/outwit-score.js multiplies
// the pool mean by (it defaults to 2/3 for the pre-2026-07-21 days that predate
// the field). House arrays are shaped around that day's fraction. Days on or
// before 2026-07-20 are frozen as shipped: two-thirds, prompt first.
